expose-system-prompts-for-local-editing

Lane: cross

Unit: reload-model-prompts-at-context-boundaries

ChildPatch: expose-system-prompts-for-local-editing

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Expose editable per-model prompt files and reload model-owned instructions when starting a new local context window without changing pinned model metadata.

Requires: Unit:cross/materialize-model-catalog-from-local-file

Provides: Seed home/instructions atomically without clobbering edits, select exact then longest-family safe filenames, retain explicit config precedence and native prompts on invalid files, and refresh model-provenance instructions in request, model-switch, and recorded incremental-tools prefixes with coherent native snapshots at window boundaries.

Boundary: Custom or inherited non-model instructions remain pinned; model catalog selection, metadata, official caches, tool declarations, context ordering, attribution, and ordinary compaction retain their native owners.

Verification: instructions_overlay and manager tests cover matching, seeding, edits, and precedence; core retained-step and model_instruction_windows tests cover unchanged within-window prompts, refreshed window prefixes, custom instructions, Responses, and Responses Lite with both tool-declaration modes.

CrossGroup: model-catalog


